% Immunosuppressive Drugs: LCD L33824 and its Policy Article A52474 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for an immunosuppressive drug (the oral and parenteral drugs of the
% J7500 series, belatacept J0485, methylprednisolone J2919, the oral
% cyclophosphamide J8530 and methotrexate J8610 when prescribed after a
% transplant, the not otherwise classified J7599) is REASONABLE AND
% NECESSARY: the statutory criteria I-IV of the Policy Article (a transplant
% of a qualifying kind — with the dated conditions of the pancreas, intestinal
% and islet cell transplants and the criteria of the pancreas transplant
% alone —, a transplant that met the Medicare coverage criteria of its time,
% Part A at the transplant, Part B at dispensing), a transplant diagnosis of
% the article's ICD-10 list, a drug whose labeling carries the rejection
% indication (or a compounded formulation of one), a regimen the treating
% practitioner finds necessary to prevent or treat rejection, the parenteral
% azathioprine and methylprednisolone only when the oral form cannot be
% tolerated or absorbed and the drug is self-administered, and at most a
% 90-day supply. The parenteral belatacept, antithymocyte globulins,
% cyclosporine and tacrolimus (J0485, J7504, J7511, J7516, J7525) are denied
% in the home setting: they are in scope and no rule concludes them.
%
% How the criteria are read. The transplant is a dated record fact (its
% organ and its date), the enrolment in Part A and Part B, the discharge, the
% mailing and the labeling of the drug are record facts; the diagnosis is a
% code of the article's table (sources/icd10/A52474_icd10_covered.csv, group
% 1, the transplant complication and status codes, serving every code of
% this policy). The findings this policy reads (dmepos.le's judged template),
% and the criterion each stands for:
%   regimen necessary to prevent rejection (the LCD: "the dosage, frequency
%   and route of administration must conform to generally accepted medical
%   practice and must be medically necessary to prevent or treat the
%   rejection of an organ transplant");
%   able to manage lifelong immunosuppression (pancreas transplant alone:
%   "able to emotionally and mentally understand the significant risks ...
%   and be able to effectively manage the lifelong need for
%   immunosuppression");
%   suitable candidate for transplantation (pancreas transplant alone:
%   "Must otherwise be a suitable candidate for transplantation").
% The HCPCS codes of the drugs are those of the article's coding guidelines
% and of the HCPCS narratives the texts cite (J7501, J2919, J0485, J7504,
% J7511, J7516, J7525, J7510, J7599, J8530, J8610); the other J75xx codes are
% the standard codes of the oral drugs, which the texts do not list. Not
% modelled: the DME MAC's own determination that an unlabeled drug is
% reasonable and necessary for rejection (a determination about the drug,
% not the beneficiary), the licensing of the dispensing entity, the supply
% fees Q0510-Q0512, the 36-month limit of the ESRD-only entitlement, the
% modifiers, the new-order rule on a change of dose.
%
% The payment conditions the policy adds (Policy Article A52474): the
% delivery requirements of criterion V (the drugs furnished on or after the
% discharge, or mailed one or two days before it with the date of service on
% the discharge), and the KX documentation (the supplier holds the transplant
% date obtained from the treating practitioner, and that date precedes the
% date of service). The article says that continued need and use are
% established by the transplant itself: this policy adds a rule for the
% shared continued need requirements accordingly.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record: the transplant
    *a beneficiary* received a transplant of *an organ* on *a date*; undefined.
    the pancreas transplant of *a beneficiary* was performed concurrent with or subsequent to a kidney transplant because of diabetic nephropathy; undefined.
    the islet cell transplant of *a beneficiary* was conducted as part of an NIH sponsored clinical trial; undefined.
    the transplant of *a beneficiary* was performed in a facility that is Medicare approved for kidney transplantation; undefined.
    the beta cell autoantibody test of *a beneficiary* is positive; undefined.
    the fasting C-peptide level of *a beneficiary* is *a number* percent of the lower limit of normal; undefined.
    the fasting glucose of *a beneficiary* obtained with the C-peptide determination is *a number* mg per dl; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was under the care of an endocrinologist with optimal and intensive management for *a number* months; undefined.
    the transplant of *a beneficiary* met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was discharged from the hospital following the transplant on *a date*; undefined.
    % the record: the drug and the supplier
    the labeling of *an item* includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ; undefined.
    *an item* is a compounded formulation of a labeled immunosuppressive drug administered orally or enterally; undefined.
    the oral form of *an item* cannot be tolerated or absorbed by *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    *an item* is self administered by the beneficiary; undefined.
    *an item* was mailed on *a date*; undefined.
    the supplier holds the transplant date of *a beneficiary* obtained from the treating practitioner; undefined.
    % the table
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table immunosuppressive_icd10.
    % derived
    *an item* is an immunosuppressive drug.
    *an item* is a parenteral drug limited to oral intolerance.
    *an item* is a parenteral drug denied in the home.
    *an item* is a covered immunosuppressive drug product.
    *an item* meets the parenteral administration criteria.
    *a beneficiary* had a covered transplant.
    the transplant of *a beneficiary* is of a qualifying kind.
    *a beneficiary* meets the pancreas transplant alone criteria.
    *a beneficiary* demonstrates insulinopenia.
    *a beneficiary* has a covered transplant diagnosis.
    *a claim* is within the 90 day supply limit.
    the delivery requirements of the transplant policy are met for *a claim*.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: group 1, the transplant complication and
% status codes, serving every code of this policy.
the table immunosuppressive_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52474_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base immunosuppressive_drugs includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base immunosuppressive_drugs includes:

LCD L33824 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33824".
the text of LCD L33824 is at "sources/lcd/L33824.txt".
Policy Article A52474 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52474".
the text of Policy Article A52474 is at "sources/article/A52474.txt".

% What the items are, by code.
rule immuno_drug with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "For all immunosuppressive drugs, the number of units billed must accurately reflect the definition of one unit of service in each code narrative":
an item is an immunosuppressive drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J7500", "J7501", "J7502", "J7503", "J7504", "J7505", "J7507", "J7508", "J7509", "J7510", "J7511", "J7512", "J7513", "J7515", "J7516", "J7517", "J7518", "J7520", "J7525", "J7527", "J7599", "J0485", "J2919", "J8530", "J8610"].

rule immuno_parenteral_home_denied with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "Parenteral belatacept (J0485), antithymocyte globulin (J7504, J7511), cyclosporine (J7516), and tacrolimus (J7525) are not proven to be safe when administered in the home setting and therefore will be denied as not medically necessary when provided in that setting":
an item is a parenteral drug denied in the home
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J0485", "J7504", "J7511", "J7516", "J7525"].

rule immuno_parenteral_limited with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "Coverage of parenteral azathioprine (J7501) or methylprednisolone (J2919) is limited to those situations in which the medication cannot be tolerated or absorbed if taken orally and is self-administered by the beneficiary":
an item is a parenteral drug limited to oral intolerance
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J7501", "J2919"].

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: the immunosuppressive
% therapy benefit of Social Security Act §1861(s)(2)(J) (Policy Article
% A52474).
rule immuno_codes with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Immunosuppressive drugs are covered under the immunosuppressive therapy benefit":
the policy for code a code is immunosuppressive_drugs
    if the code is in ["J7500", "J7501", "J7502", "J7503", "J7504", "J7505", "J7507", "J7508", "J7509", "J7510", "J7511", "J7512", "J7513", "J7515", "J7516", "J7517", "J7518", "J7520", "J7525", "J7527", "J7599", "J0485", "J2919", "J8530", "J8610"].

rule immuno_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Immunosuppressive drugs are covered under the immunosuppressive therapy benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is immunosuppressive therapy benefit
    if the policy for code the code is immunosuppressive_drugs.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The drug: a covered transplant, a transplant diagnosis, a labeled drug, a
% regimen the practitioner finds necessary, at most a 90-day supply.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule immuno_claim with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "For immunosuppressive drugs covered under this policy, the dosage, frequency and route of administration must conform to generally accepted medical practice and must be medically necessary to prevent or treat the rejection of an organ transplant":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an immunosuppressive drug
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a parenteral drug limited to oral intolerance
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a parenteral drug denied in the home
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary had a covered transplant
    and the beneficiary has a covered transplant diagnosis
    and the item is a covered immunosuppressive drug product
    and the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about the beneficiary is established
    and the claim is within the 90 day supply limit.

rule immuno_claim_parenteral with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "Coverage of parenteral azathioprine (J7501) or methylprednisolone (J2919) is limited to those situations in which the medication cannot be tolerated or absorbed if taken orally and is self-administered by the beneficiary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a parenteral drug limited to oral intolerance
    and the item meets the parenteral administration criteria
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary had a covered transplant
    and the beneficiary has a covered transplant diagnosis
    and the item is a covered immunosuppressive drug product
    and the finding regimen necessary to prevent rejection about the beneficiary is established
    and the claim is within the 90 day supply limit.

rule immuno_parenteral_criteria with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "limited to those situations in which the medication cannot be tolerated or absorbed if taken orally and is self-administered by the beneficiary":
an item meets the parenteral administration criteria
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the oral form of the item cannot be tolerated or absorbed by the beneficiary
    and the item is self administered by the beneficiary.

% The covered drug: FDA-approved with the rejection indication in its
% labeling, or a compounded oral or enteral formulation of such a drug.
rule immuno_labeled_drug with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "The approved labeling includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ or tissue":
an item is a covered immunosuppressive drug product
    if the labeling of the item includes an indication for preventing or treating the rejection of a transplanted organ.

rule immuno_compounded_drug with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "The drug is a compounded formulation derived only from a drug described in paragraph (1) or (2) of this section and is orally or enterally administered":
an item is a covered immunosuppressive drug product
    if the item is a compounded formulation of a labeled immunosuppressive drug administered orally or enterally.

rule immuno_supply_limit with provenance LCD L33824,
        confer "The quantity of immunosuppressive drugs dispensed is limited to a 90-day supply":
a claim is within the 90 day supply limit
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 3.

% The diagnosis: a transplant code of the article's list.
rule immuno_diagnosis with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "The diagnosis code(s) that justify the need for these items must be included on the claim. See the below list for covered transplant diagnosis codes":
a beneficiary has a covered transplant diagnosis
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52474" as a description under table immunosuppressive_icd10.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The covered transplant: criteria I, II and III of the Policy Article.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule immuno_covered_transplant with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "If criteria I, II, and III are met, the transplant is considered a":
a beneficiary had a covered transplant
    if the transplant of the beneficiary is of a qualifying kind
    and the transplant of the beneficiary met the Medicare coverage criteria in effect at the time
    and the beneficiary was enrolled in Medicare Part A at the time of the transplant
    and the beneficiary is enrolled in Medicare Part B at the time the drugs are dispensed.

rule immuno_transplant_organ with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Kidney, heart, liver, bone marrow/stem cell, lung, or heart/lung transplant":
the transplant of a beneficiary is of a qualifying kind
    if the beneficiary received a transplant of an organ on a date
    and the organ is in [kidney, heart, liver, bone marrow, stem cell, lung, heart lung].

rule immuno_transplant_pancreas_with_kidney with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Whole organ pancreas transplant performed concurrent with or subsequent to a kidney transplant because of diabetic nephropathy (performed on or after July 1, 1999)":
the transplant of a beneficiary is of a qualifying kind
    if the beneficiary received a transplant of whole organ pancreas on a date
    and the pancreas transplant of the beneficiary was performed concurrent with or subsequent to a kidney transplant because of diabetic nephropathy
    and the date is after or equal to 1999-07-01.

rule immuno_transplant_intestinal with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Intestinal transplant (performed on or after April 1, 2001)":
the transplant of a beneficiary is of a qualifying kind
    if the beneficiary received a transplant of intestine on a date
    and the date is after or equal to 2001-04-01.

rule immuno_transplant_islet with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Pancreatic islet cell transplant or partial pancreatic tissue transplantation performed on or after October 1, 2004 that is conducted as part of a National Institutes of Health (NIH)-sponsored clinical trial":
the transplant of a beneficiary is of a qualifying kind
    if the beneficiary received a transplant of an organ on a date
    and the organ is in [pancreatic islet cell, partial pancreatic tissue]
    and the islet cell transplant of the beneficiary was conducted as part of an NIH sponsored clinical trial
    and the date is after or equal to 2004-10-01.

rule immuno_transplant_pancreas_alone with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Pancreas transplants alone (performed on or after April 26, 2006) that meet the following criteria":
the transplant of a beneficiary is of a qualifying kind
    if the beneficiary received a transplant of pancreas alone on a date
    and the date is after or equal to 2006-04-26
    and the beneficiary meets the pancreas transplant alone criteria.

rule immuno_pancreas_alone_criteria with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "The transplant is performed in a facility that is Medicare-approved for kidney transplantation":
a beneficiary meets the pancreas transplant alone criteria
    if the transplant of the beneficiary was performed in a facility that is Medicare approved for kidney transplantation
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents type I diabetes
    and the beneficiary demonstrates insulinopenia
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents labile insulin dependent diabetes with hospitalization
    and the beneficiary was under the care of an endocrinologist with optimal and intensive management for a number months
    and the number >= 12
    and the finding able to manage lifelong immunosuppression about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding suitable candidate for transplantation about the beneficiary is established.

rule immuno_autoantibody with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Must be beta cell autoantibody positive":
a beneficiary demonstrates insulinopenia
    if the beta cell autoantibody test of the beneficiary is positive.

% the garbled sentence of the text ("is 225 mg/dL") is read as the
% original's "less than or equal to 225 mg/dL"
rule immuno_c_peptide with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "Must demonstrate insulinopenia, (fasting C-peptide level that is less than or equal to 110% of the lower limit of normal of the laboratory's measurement method)":
a beneficiary demonstrates insulinopenia
    if the fasting C-peptide level of the beneficiary is a number percent of the lower limit of normal
    and the number <= 110
    and the fasting glucose of the beneficiary obtained with the C-peptide determination is an other number mg per dl
    and the other number <= 225.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment: the KX documentation (the supplier
% holds the transplant date from the practitioner, and it precedes the date
% of service) and the delivery requirements of criterion V.
rule immuno_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "The supplier has obtained from the treating practitioner the specific date of the organ transplant":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is immunosuppressive_drugs
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the supplier holds the transplant date of the beneficiary obtained from the treating practitioner
    and the beneficiary received a transplant of an organ on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the date is before the other date
    and the delivery requirements of the transplant policy are met for the claim.

rule immuno_delivery_after_discharge with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "the drugs are furnished on or after the date of discharge from the hospital following a covered organ transplant":
the delivery requirements of the transplant policy are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary was discharged from the hospital following the transplant on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is after or equal to the date.

rule immuno_delivery_mailed_before_discharge with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "mail-order deliveries may be mailed one or two days prior to a beneficiary’s anticipated date of discharge from an inpatient facility to a qualified place of service or alternate address":
the delivery requirements of the transplant policy are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary was discharged from the hospital following the transplant on a date
    and the item was mailed on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 1
    and the number <= 2
    and the date of service of the claim is the date.

% Continued need and use are established by the transplant: no further record
% of continued need is required for a claim of this policy (an addition to
% the shared continued need rules of dmepos.le).
rule immuno_continued_need with provenance Policy Article A52474,
        confer "There is no requirement for further documentation of continued need for the life of the transplant":
the continued need requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is immunosuppressive_drugs
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary had a covered transplant.
